#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_map

#% text
# `key_map(f, a)` gives the association `a` with every key `k` replaced by `f(k)`; the values stay. `key_map(f)` is the operator form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_map(f, assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2))
#% output
#= assoc(f(a) -> 1, f(b) -> 2)

#% cell
key_map(to_upper, assoc("x" -> 1, "y" -> 2))
#% output
#= assoc("X" -> 1, "Y" -> 2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_value_map`, `map_values`
